<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarahan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarahan is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimla">Shimla</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, high above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> valley. It was the summer seat of the Rajas of Bashahr, whose palace stands there. Its Bhimakali temple, built in a distinctive Himalayan style of wood and stone, was the family shrine of the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarahan.jpg" alt="Sarahan" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sanyam Bahga · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinnaur_048.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
